  "environment_caveats": [
    "Staging Cloudflare Pages preview returns x-robots-tag: noindex, so the Lighthouse is-crawlable audit fails on all 6 URLs and deflates the SEO category to 69. SEO is recorded but EXCLUDED from all verdicts this run. Status: inconclusive - staging noindex artifact, re-audit after apex cutover.",
    "Canonicals correctly point to the future apex (https://tdiusa.com/...), not to the staging host. This is expected pre-cutover and is NOT counted as an offsite-canonical defect. Note that tdiusa.com currently 302-redirects to www.buildwithtdi.com (old Scorpion site) until cutover completes.",
    "DataForSEO instant_pages returned has_micromarkup=false, but JSON-LD (Organization, WebSite, LocalBusiness) is present and parses on every page - verified directly against served HTML. Treated as a DataForSEO false negative, not a missing-schema defect.",
    "Client record status is \"onboarding\", not \"active\". Audit proceeded because the pipeline System 3 gate (scripts/master_scheduler.py:290) keys on build_status (pushed_main), and crew-restoration-construction (also onboarding) was audited 2026-08-26 under the same gate.",
    "Lighthouse 13.4.0 adds an \"agentic-browsing\" category not in this methodology; recorded per URL as agentic_browsing_score but excluded from verdicts.",
    "on_page_lighthouse / on_page_instant_pages MCP tools are absent from this MCP build; endpoints were called directly via /v3/on_page/lighthouse/live/json and /v3/on_page/instant_pages. The raw API DOES expose for_mobile, so mobile-form-factor auditing is now possible if the methodology adopts it; this run used for_mobile=false for consistency with prior desktop audits."
